    "what_each_does": {
      ".claude/commands/chore.md": "The chore-planning template (53 lines): meta prompt that turns a one-line chore into a specs/*.md plan using the exact Plan Format (Chore / Description / Relevant Files / Step by Step Tasks / Validation Commands / Notes). $ARGUMENTS at the bottom receives your string.",
      ".claude/commands/bug.md": "The bug-planning template (69 lines): adds Problem/Solution Statements, Steps to Reproduce, Root Cause Analysis; instructions demand a surgical, minimal fix ('Don't use decorators. Keep it simple.'), uv add for new libs reported in Notes.",
      ".claude/commands/feature.md": "The feature-planning template (91 lines): adds User Story, 3-phase Implementation Plan, Testing Strategy, Acceptance Criteria; instructions demand researching existing patterns and designing for extensibility.",
      ".claude/commands/implement.md": "The universal executor HOP (12 displayed lines): 'Read the plan, think hard about the plan and implement the plan' + ## Plan $ARGUMENTS + ## Report (bullet summary, git diff --stat). Runs ANY spec the templates generate.",
      ".claude/commands/install.md": "Setup meta-command: reads+executes prime.md, installs FE and BE dependencies, runs ./scripts/copy_dot_env.sh to copy the .env from the tac-2 directory, reports work — the lesson's first example of agentic reuse.",
      ".claude/commands/prime.md": "Context priming: run git ls-files, read README.md, summarize understanding — the standard TAC boot ritual carried forward from lesson 2.",
      ".claude/commands/start.md": "One line: 'sh ./scripts/start.sh 300s' — agent-runnable app boot.",
      ".claude/commands/tools.md": "Utility prompt: list all built-in tools in TypeScript function syntax — the introspection command from lesson 2.",
      ".claude/settings.json": "Permission config with a new twist vs tac-1: an allow list of 12 entries (Bash mkdir/uv/find/mv/grep/npm/ls/cp/chmod/touch wildcards, Write, and Bash(./scripts/copy_dot_env.sh:*)) PLUS an explicit deny list: Bash(git push --force:*), Bash(git push -f:*), Bash(rm -rf:*) — the course's first on-disk guardrails against destructive commands.",
      "README.md": "The Natural Language SQL Interface docs (from lesson 2): setup, scripts, API endpoints, project structure — and the file every template tells the agent to read first. Its Security section still advertises 'SQL injection protection via keyword blocking', which is precisely the inadequate defense the /bug demo replaces.",
      "app/server/server.py": "FastAPI app (258 lines) with upload/query/schema/insights/health/delete_table endpoints — ships with 18 print() lines (the /chore target) and a genuine injection surface: cursor.execute(f\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS {table_name}\") at line 243.",
      "app/server/main.py": "6-line hello stub with the 19th print statement.",
      "app/server/core/sql_processor.py": "execute_sql_safely(): substring blocklist of 10 dangerous keywords, then executes the raw query string — no parameterization (the bug's root cause); get_database_schema() f-strings table names into PRAGMA/COUNT queries.",
      "app/server/core/llm_processor.py": "NL→SQL via OpenAI (gpt-4.1-mini) or Anthropic with schema-aware prompts — user natural language becomes executable SQL, the other half of the injection surface.",
      "app/server/core/file_processor.py": "CSV/JSON → SQLite via pandas; sanitize_table_name() regex-cleans table names (the partial mitigation the bug plan builds on).",
      "app/server/core/insights.py": "Column insights generation (f-string SQL over table/column names — cited in the bug plan's relevant files).",
      "app/server/tests/": "37 pre-existing test functions across test_file_processor (9), test_llm_processor (16), test_sql_processor (12) — the regression floor the plans' Validation Commands protect.",
      "scripts/copy_dot_env.sh": "Copies ../tac-2/app/server/.env into app/server/.env (fails loudly if tac-2 isn't a sibling) — invoked agentically by /install.",
      "scripts/start.sh / scripts/stop_apps.sh": "Boot both services with .env checks and graceful shutdown / kill by port (5173, 8000).",
      "adws/README.md + agents/README.md": "Empty placeholder directories — the slots where AI developer workflows and agent definitions land in later lessons; their emptiness IS the lesson-4 teaser on disk.",
      "ai_docs/": "Cached Anthropic/OpenAI quick-start docs for agent context (context-priming resource, carried from lesson 2).",
      "specs/init_nlq_to_sql_to_table.md": "The 749-line initial plan that BUILT this entire app in lesson 2 — living proof of 'plans are prompts scaled up' sitting in the repo before you type anything.",
      ".env.sample": "OPENAI_API_KEY= / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY= placeholders (root); app/server/.env.sample is the one the server loads via python-dotenv."
    },
    "generated_not_committed": {
      "specs/replace-print-with-logging.md": "The chore plan (64 lines) generated on camera from one sentence — inventories every print by line number and prescribes logger.info/logger.error with a preserved [SUCCESS]/[ERROR] format.",
      "specs/fix-sql-injection-vulnerabilities.md": "The bug plan generated on camera: full root-cause analysis and a New Files section creating app/server/core/sql_security.py.",
      "specs/query-history-panel.md": "The feature plan generated HEADLESSLY by the claude -p run — reviewed on camera, deliberately left unimplemented.",
      "app/server/core/sql_security.py": "Centralized SQL security utilities (identifier validation, safe execution) created by the bug implement run.",
      "test_sql_injection.py (+ manual test script)": "18 new SQL-injection prevention tests created by the bug implement run; video shows 52 tests passing afterward.",
      "feature_plan_raw_agent_logs.jsonl": "The live-streamed JSONL of the headless feature-planning agent (model claude-opus-4-20250514 visible in events).",
      "app/server/.env": "Copied from ../tac-2 by the /install → copy_dot_env.sh step.",
      "logging changes across server.py/main.py": "The chore implement run's diff: every print( replaced by logger calls with levels, stdout preserved."
    }
