+# TAC-3 Chapter Status: DONE ✅
+
+## Deliverables
+
+- `03-success-is-planned.html` — complete teaching-first TAC-3 chapter
+- `03-success-is-planned.assets.css` — chapter layout, diagrams, large-frame treatment, responsive behavior, and print rules
+- `../index.html` — shared hub currently links TAC-3 and counts all four built TAC chapters
+- `../data/curriculum.json` — TAC-3 marked `chaptered` with tactic, extract, chapter, density, and overlay metadata
+
+## Density estimate
+
+- **Visible teaching text:** **10,353 words** from HTML text extraction, excluding CSS and JavaScript
+- **Print-equivalent estimate:** **38–45 dense pages**
+- Estimate basis: 10 complete ten-move pedagogy cycles, 14 teaching-frame placements from 12 unique native frames, 9 designed HTML systems diagrams, 12 evidence/comparison/file maps, 12 graded lab/checkpoint blocks, 38 answer disclosures, cumulative mastery, and a 22-term glossary. Figures, code, tables, and callouts reduce words per page relative to plain prose.
+
+## Requirement coverage
+
+- All 10 extract-defined major ideas implement Hook → Picture → Story/frame → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval `<details>` → Teach-back
+- Sticky chapter rail, dual reading progress, active-section highlighting, mobile TOC, responsive collapse, and print rules included
+- Light/offline-first design uses `../design/tokens.css`, `base.css`, `components.css`, and local lesson CSS; no CDN dependency
+- Frames render in full-width cards at up to 1100px with `object-fit: contain`, native `1920×1080` dimensions, meaningful alt text, and timestamp captions
+- HTML diagrams cover the scaling ladder, class-specific templates, meta-prompt expansion, HOP composition, reasoning fan-out, fresh-agent split, KPIs, validation loop, interactive/headless symmetry, and specialization flywheel
+- Course facts are separated from observed generated demo outputs; 19 print calls and 37 pre-existing tests are treated as disk truth, while 20 prints and 52/18 tests are identified as narration/run-specific
+- Required lab uses only the TAC-3 course repository; the extract’s home-repo porting stretch was intentionally omitted to respect the brief
+- Lab includes setup, chore plan/build, bug plan/build, headless feature planning, course-repo stretches, troubleshooting, graded checkpoints, and a final pass sheet
+- Two extract-approved YouTube overlays are included; the third candidate remains deferred
+- Glossary, cumulative retrieval, scoring, and capstone teach-back included
+
+## Verification completed
+
+- Extract `STATUS.md` exists and reports DONE; no blocker file was needed
+- All local CSS, frame, hub, and fragment paths resolve from the chapter path
+- No duplicate HTML IDs or broken internal anchors
+- Exactly 10 idea cycles and exactly 100 pedagogy moves: 10 of each required move type
+- All 12 referenced frame files exist and report native `1920×1080` dimensions
+- Curriculum JSON parses after the TAC-3 update
+- Chapter inline JavaScript passes syntax validation; scroll work is animation-frame gated
+- CSS braces balance; no inline style attributes remain in the chapter
+- Course-file claims cross-checked against the extract’s verified codebase map and lab spec
+- Hub reflects the actual shared workspace state: TAC chapters 1–4 linked, 4 of 18 overall, 4 of 8 in Volume I
+
+## Open questions for Claude cross-review
+
+1. Reverify the two YouTube IDs/titles and every mid-2026 current-practice claim at publication; the extract explicitly marks these as time-sensitive and no TAC-3-specific seed list was supplied.
+2. Visually inspect desktop sticky rail, 65rem/46rem breakpoints, 1100px frame clarity, diagram wrapping, and print pagination in a normal browser. The in-app browser could not start in this sandbox, and local Chrome did not emit a screenshot; static DOM/CSS/path checks passed.
+3. Sanity-check the **38–45 page** print estimate against the project’s final print engine and margins.
+4. Decide whether the optional course-repo two-node headless stretch should remain in this chapter or move wholly into TAC-4; it is clearly labeled optional and permission-bounded here.
+5. Confirm that repeating the t0660 frame for the reasoning section and t2575 for specialization is pedagogically preferable to leaving those story beats unframed; all 12 unique extract frames are used at least once.
+
+## Known blockers
+
+None.
