IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:177:        <div class="move move--example"><p class="move-label">5 · Worked example — grade invariants, not magic totals</p><h3>Logging and SQL require different evidence</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Calibration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Regression-free baseline</td><td><code>cd app/server &amp;&amp; uv run pytest</code></td><td>The shipped repo collects 34 tests. There are 37 <code>test_*</code> definitions, but three are fixtures.</td></tr><tr><td>No raw server prints</td><td><code>rg -n 'print\(' app/server/server.py app/server/main.py</code></td><td>Require zero hits after the “all server prints” chore.</td></tr><tr><td>Message semantics preserved</td><td>Direct behavior or app run shows the same <code>[SUCCESS]</code>/<code>[ERROR]</code> payload shapes on stdout.</td><td>Do not infer this from pytest unless a test asserts it.</td></tr><tr><td>SQL risk reduced</td><td>New focused cases exercise raw query and identifier surfaces; all baseline tests remain green.</td><td>Dan’s 18-new/52-total result is one run, not the grading constant.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:181:        <div class="move move--check"><p class="move-label">9 · Retrieval check</p><section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Validation retrieval"><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">Name two self-validation mechanisms shown in the lesson.</p><details><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Plan-embedded Validation Commands and the agent’s review of its own diff followed by fixes.</p></details></div><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">What does the human still do?</p><details><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Inspect the plan/diff and independently repeat key behavior or reproduction plus the test command.</p></details></div><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">What is the real shipped baseline test count?</p><details><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>34 collected tests. The 37 test-named functions include three pytest fixtures.</p></details></div></section></div>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:189:        <div class="move move--story"><p class="move-label">3 · Story — a plan appears without an interactive agent</p><h3>Command, heartbeat, deliverable</h3><p>Dan runs the feature template in Claude Code’s programmatic form, selects stream JSON, bypasses permissions for this narrowly scoped demo, chooses an Opus model, requests verbose output, and redirects the stream into <code>feature_plan_raw_agent_logs.jsonl</code>. The file appends system, assistant, and tool-result events. The model visible in the captured JSONL is <code>claude-opus-4-20250514</code>.</p><figure class="frame-card"><img src="../media/frames/tac-3-success-is-planned/t2205-claude-p-command.png" alt="Course frame showing the complete claude -p feature planning command and flags" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">36:45</span>The full headless command turns the existing <code>/feature</code> template into a callable planning phase.</figcaption></figure><figure class="frame-card"><img src="../media/frames/tac-3-success-is-planned/t2270-jsonl-stream-live.png" alt="Course frame showing JSONL system assistant and tool events appending live" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">37:50</span>The JSONL is not decorative logging. It is the event interface another program can parse while the planner runs.</figcaption></figure><figure class="frame-card"><img src="../media/frames/tac-3-success-is-planned/t2575-feature-spec-query-history.png" alt="Course frame showing the generated query history side panel feature plan" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy"><figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">42:55</span>The planning-only run leaves a feature spec with Feature Description, User Story, and Problem Statement. Dan reviews it but does not implement it.</figcaption></figure></div>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:232:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Checkpoint 1A pass</h4><ul><li>□ A new plan exists under <code>specs/</code>.</li><li>□ Its inventory includes <code>app/server/server.py</code> and <code>app/server/main.py</code>.</li><li>□ You reconcile the disk truth as 18 + 1 = 19 print calls rather than copying the video agent’s off-by-one prose.</li><li>□ The plan preserves the <code>[SUCCESS]</code>/<code>[ERROR]</code> message shapes and stdout behavior.</li><li>□ The plan contains the seeded pytest command and a final validation step.</li></ul></div>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:237:          <ol class="lab-box__steps"><li>Run <code>cd app/server &amp;&amp; uv run pytest</code>; require zero regressions against the 34 tests pytest actually collects. The 37 <code>test_*</code> function definitions include three fixtures.</li><li>Search the two target files with <code>rg -n 'print\(' app/server/server.py app/server/main.py</code>. Because the request says <em>all server print statements</em>, require zero hits across both files.</li><li>Restart through <code>scripts/start.sh</code>, then ask <strong>get users id name sorted by signup date descending</strong>.</li><li>Confirm the same success/error message shapes flow through logging to stdout.</li><li>Read the agent’s report. It must contain concise bullets plus <code>git diff --stat</code>.</li></ol>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/03-success-is-planned.html:279:        <h3>Round 3 · Diagnose failures</h3><section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Diagnosis mastery"><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">9. A build succeeds only when run in the same planning conversation. What failed?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The plan has a hidden conversational dependency and is not a zero-dependency reusable asset.</p></details></div><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">10. A copied template searches directories that do not exist. What should change?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The template’s Relevant Files and validation seed must be rewritten for the actual repository before generating plans.</p></details></div><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">11. An agent reports 20 print calls; the line inventory and disk show 19. What do you trust?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The enumerated, independently checked repository evidence: 18 in <code>server.py</code> and one in <code>main.py</code>.</p></details></div><div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">12. A bug run has fewer than 52 tests but adds targeted coverage and has zero regressions. Pass or fail?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Potentially pass. The 52/18 numbers describe one generated run; grade the invariants and evidence.</p></details></div></section>
