 ## Density estimate
 
-- **Visible teaching text:** **10,506 words** from HTML text extraction, excluding CSS and JavaScript
-- **Print-equivalent estimate:** **38–45 dense pages**
-- Estimate basis: 10 complete ten-move pedagogy cycles, 14 teaching-frame placements from 12 unique native frames, 9 designed HTML systems diagrams, 12 evidence/comparison/file maps, 12 graded lab/checkpoint blocks, 38 answer disclosures, cumulative mastery, and a 22-term glossary. Figures, code, tables, and callouts reduce words per page relative to plain prose.
+- Visible chapter words: **10,365** (HTML text excluding script/style)
+- Source HTML: **318 lines** (dense component markup)
+- Estimated print-equivalent pages: **38–44**, based on roughly 235–275 teaching words/page plus 14 full-width frame uses, diagrams, tables, retrieval disclosures, and lab checkpoints
+- Teaching cycles: **10 × 10 required moves = 100 moves**
+- Retrieval disclosures: **41**
+- Glossary entries: **22**
+
+## Source grounding
 
+- Extract readiness: `_extracts/tac-3-success-is-planned/STATUS.md` exists and is DONE; blocked-path rule did not apply.
+- Consumed all extract deliverables: `extract.md`, `extract.json`, `nuggets.md`, `frame-plan.json`, `lab-spec.md`, `outdated-vs-current.md`, and `STATUS.md`.
+- Lab uses only the standalone TAC-3 course repository and real shipped paths.
+- All 12 selected source frames appear large; two are deliberately reused where one frame supports a second concept. Every source frame is 1920×1080.
+- Generated-on-camera artifacts are described as observed outcomes, not falsely claimed as files shipped in the baseline repository.
+
+## Countable-fact corrections
+
+- Logging baseline: **18** `print(` calls in `app/server/server.py` + **1** in `app/server/main.py` = **19**. The on-camera agent’s “20” prose is not repeated as repository truth.
+- Test baseline: pytest collects **34 tests**. The repository has **37 `def test_*` symbols**, but three are fixtures. The chapter and graded lab use 34 collected as the regression floor.
+- Dan’s post-fix **52 total / 18 new** is labeled run-specific; grading requires new injection-focused cases and zero regressions, not a magic total or filename.
+- `implement.md` displays 12 lines but `wc -l` reports 11 because there is no trailing newline; both facts are explained.
+
 ## Requirement coverage
 
-- All 10 extract-defined major ideas implement Hook → Picture → Story/frame → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval `<details>` → Teach-back
-- Sticky chapter rail, dual reading progress, active-section highlighting, mobile TOC, responsive collapse, and print rules included
-- Light/offline-first design uses `../design/tokens.css`, `base.css`, `components.css`, and local lesson CSS; no CDN dependency
-- Frames render in full-width cards at up to 1100px with `object-fit: contain`, native `1920×1080` dimensions, meaningful alt text, and timestamp captions
-- HTML diagrams cover the scaling ladder, class-specific templates, meta-prompt expansion, HOP composition, reasoning fan-out, fresh-agent split, KPIs, validation loop, interactive/headless symmetry, and specialization flywheel
-- Course facts are separated from observed generated demo outputs; 19 print calls and 37 pre-existing tests are treated as disk truth, while 20 prints and 52/18 tests are identified as narration/run-specific
-- Required lab uses only the TAC-3 course repository; the extract’s home-repo porting stretch was intentionally omitted to respect the brief
-- Lab includes setup, chore plan/build, bug plan/build, headless feature planning, course-repo stretches, troubleshooting, graded checkpoints, and a final pass sheet
-- Two extract-approved YouTube overlays are included; the third candidate remains deferred
-- Glossary, cumulative retrieval, scoring, and capstone teach-back included
+- Light, high-contrast, offline-first theme using `design/tokens.css`, `base.css`, and `components.css`: ✅
+- Desktop sticky rail, mobile TOC, reading progress, active-section navigation: ✅
+- Frames full-width up to 1100px, `object-fit: contain`, descriptive alt text, timestamp captions: ✅
+- Hook → Picture → Story → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval → Teach-back for all 10 ideas: ✅
