-# TAC-3 Chapter Status: DONE ✅
+# STATUS: CHAPTERED ✅
+
+TAC-3 · **Success is Planned** · lesson key `tac-3-success-is-planned`
 
 ## Deliverables
 
-- `03-success-is-planned.html` — complete teaching-first TAC-3 chapter
-- `03-success-is-planned.assets.css` — chapter layout, diagrams, large-frame treatment, responsive behavior, and print rules
-- `../index.html` — shared hub currently links TAC-3 and counts all four built TAC chapters
-- `../data/curriculum.json` — TAC-3 marked `chaptered` with tactic, extract, chapter, density, and overlay metadata
+| File | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `03-success-is-planned.html` | Complete teaching chapter: orientation, 10 major idea cycles, graded course-repo lab, cumulative mastery, glossary, sticky navigation, progress, and previous/next links |
+| `03-success-is-planned.assets.css` | Complete light-theme chapter layout using shared tokens/base/components; responsive rail/TOC, full-width teaching frames, diagrams, lab UI, reduced motion, and print rules |
+| `../index.html` | TAC-3 linked; hub synchronized to 4/18 overall and 4/8 TAC |
+| `../data/curriculum.json` | TAC-3 marked `chaptered` with extract, chapter, tactic, estimates, and two approved current-practice overlays |
 
 ## Density estimate
 
-- **Visible teaching text:** **10,506 words** from HTML text extraction, excluding CSS and JavaScript
-- **Print-equivalent estimate:** **38–45 dense pages**
-- Estimate basis: 10 complete ten-move pedagogy cycles, 14 teaching-frame placements from 12 unique native frames, 9 designed HTML systems diagrams, 12 evidence/comparison/file maps, 12 graded lab/checkpoint blocks, 38 answer disclosures, cumulative mastery, and a 22-term glossary. Figures, code, tables, and callouts reduce words per page relative to plain prose.
+- Visible chapter words: **10,365** (HTML text excluding script/style)
+- Source HTML: **318 lines** (dense component markup)
+- Estimated print-equivalent pages: **38–44**, based on roughly 235–275 teaching words/page plus 14 full-width frame uses, diagrams, tables, retrieval disclosures, and lab checkpoints
+- Teaching cycles: **10 × 10 required moves = 100 moves**
+- Retrieval disclosures: **41**
+- Glossary entries: **22**
+
+## Source grounding
 
+- Extract readiness: `_extracts/tac-3-success-is-planned/STATUS.md` exists and is DONE; blocked-path rule did not apply.
+- Consumed all extract deliverables: `extract.md`, `extract.json`, `nuggets.md`, `frame-plan.json`, `lab-spec.md`, `outdated-vs-current.md`, and `STATUS.md`.
+- Lab uses only the standalone TAC-3 course repository and real shipped paths.
+- All 12 selected source frames appear large; two are deliberately reused where one frame supports a second concept. Every source frame is 1920×1080.
+- Generated-on-camera artifacts are described as observed outcomes, not falsely claimed as files shipped in the baseline repository.
+
+## Countable-fact corrections
+
+- Logging baseline: **18** `print(` calls in `app/server/server.py` + **1** in `app/server/main.py` = **19**. The on-camera agent’s “20” prose is not repeated as repository truth.
+- Test baseline: pytest collects **34 tests**. The repository has **37 `def test_*` symbols**, but three are fixtures. The chapter and graded lab use 34 collected as the regression floor.
+- Dan’s post-fix **52 total / 18 new** is labeled run-specific; grading requires new injection-focused cases and zero regressions, not a magic total or filename.
+- `implement.md` displays 12 lines but `wc -l` reports 11 because there is no trailing newline; both facts are explained.
+
 ## Requirement coverage
 
-- All 10 extract-defined major ideas implement Hook → Picture → Story/frame → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval `<details>` → Teach-back
-- Sticky chapter rail, dual reading progress, active-section highlighting, mobile TOC, responsive collapse, and print rules included
-- Light/offline-first design uses `../design/tokens.css`, `base.css`, `components.css`, and local lesson CSS; no CDN dependency
-- Frames render in full-width cards at up to 1100px with `object-fit: contain`, native `1920×1080` dimensions, meaningful alt text, and timestamp captions
-- HTML diagrams cover the scaling ladder, class-specific templates, meta-prompt expansion, HOP composition, reasoning fan-out, fresh-agent split, KPIs, validation loop, interactive/headless symmetry, and specialization flywheel
-- Course facts are separated from observed generated demo outputs; 19 print calls and 37 pre-existing tests are treated as disk truth, while 20 prints and 52/18 tests are identified as narration/run-specific
-- Required lab uses only the TAC-3 course repository; the extract’s home-repo porting stretch was intentionally omitted to respect the brief
-- Lab includes setup, chore plan/build, bug plan/build, headless feature planning, course-repo stretches, troubleshooting, graded checkpoints, and a final pass sheet
-- Two extract-approved YouTube overlays are included; the third candidate remains deferred
-- Glossary, cumulative retrieval, scoring, and capstone teach-back included
+- Light, high-contrast, offline-first theme using `design/tokens.css`, `base.css`, and `components.css`: ✅
+- Desktop sticky rail, mobile TOC, reading progress, active-section navigation: ✅
+- Frames full-width up to 1100px, `object-fit: contain`, descriptive alt text, timestamp captions: ✅
+- Hook → Picture → Story → Name → Worked example → You try → Fail/fix → Current Practice → Retrieval → Teach-back for all 10 ideas: ✅
+- Current-practice YouTube limit: **2**, both approved by the extract: ✅
+- Graded lab, safety/scoping, deterministic evidence, troubleshooting, final pass sheet: ✅
+- Cumulative mastery and glossary: ✅
+- Hub link/progress and curriculum metadata: ✅
+
+## Verification performed
+
+- All 22 local CSS/image/navigation paths resolved from the chapter directory; no missing files.
+- All 28 fragment links resolve; no duplicate HTML IDs.
+- Desktop rail and mobile TOC contain the same 14 anchors in the same order.
+- Each of the 10 idea sections contains exactly one of every required move class.
+- Inline JavaScript compiles with Node; linked JSON parses with `jq`.
+- Chapter and shared CSS files have balanced braces.
+- All 12 unique frame files exist and report native 1920×1080 dimensions.
+- Responsive CSS hides the rail/shows the mobile TOC at 65rem, stacks grids at 46rem, and preserves ≥17px shared body typography.
+- Two-axis final review found no high-severity issues; mobile table scrolling, print-visible retrieval answers, keyboard skip navigation, observer progressive enhancement, and source-bounded current-practice wording were repaired.
+- Browser-skill interactive QA was attempted but the sandbox could not initialize the in-app browser; the preinstalled Chrome binary also did not produce a headless screenshot in this managed environment. Static/semantic/path checks above completed successfully.
 
-## Verification completed
+## Intentional lab calibration
 
-- Extract `STATUS.md` exists and reports DONE; no blocker file was needed
-- All local CSS, frame, hub, and fragment paths resolve from the chapter path
-- No duplicate HTML IDs or broken internal anchors
-- Exactly 10 idea cycles and exactly 100 pedagogy moves: 10 of each required move type
-- All 12 referenced frame files exist and report native `1920×1080` dimensions
-- Curriculum JSON parses after the TAC-3 update
-- Chapter inline JavaScript passes syntax validation; scroll work is animation-frame gated
-- CSS braces balance; no inline style attributes remain in the chapter
-- Course-file claims cross-checked against the extract’s verified codebase map and lab spec
-- Hub reflects the actual shared workspace state: TAC chapters 1–4 linked, 4 of 18 overall, 4 of 8 in Volume I
+The extract’s draft lab required a new injection test **file** and made an LLM-mediated UI injection attempt part of the pass. The final chapter grades new injection-focused **cases** in either an existing or new test module and uses deterministic direct tests as the security pass, with UI reproduction supplemental. This is an intentional course-code-grounded correction: test location is not the invariant, and UI natural-language-to-SQL translation depends on external credentials and nondeterministic model output.
 
-## Open questions for Claude cross-review
+## Open questions for Claude review
 
-1. Reverify the two YouTube IDs/titles and every mid-2026 current-practice claim at publication; the extract explicitly marks these as time-sensitive and no TAC-3-specific seed list was supplied.
-2. Visually inspect desktop sticky rail, 65rem/46rem breakpoints, 1100px frame clarity, diagram wrapping, and print pagination in a normal browser. The in-app browser could not start in this sandbox, and local Chrome did not emit a screenshot; static DOM/CSS/path checks passed.
-3. Sanity-check the **38–45 page** print estimate against the project’s final print engine and margins.
-4. Decide whether the optional course-repo two-node headless stretch should remain in this chapter or move wholly into TAC-4; it is clearly labeled optional and permission-bounded here.
-5. Confirm that repeating the t0660 frame for the reasoning section and t2575 for specialization is pedagogically preferable to leaving those story beats unframed; all 12 unique extract frames are used at least once.
+1. Does the 10,506-word / 38–45-page density feel equivalent to TAC-1 gold, or should any idea receive another worked case rather than more prose?
+2. Should the historical `--dangerously-skip-permissions` lab reproduction remain required-but-narrowly-scoped, or become an optional exact-reproduction path with scoped permissions as the default?
+3. The two current-practice YouTube IDs were approved in the extract but reused from TAC-1’s verified seed list because no TAC-3-specific seed list existed. Replace if a dedicated planning/spec video becomes available.
+4. Re-verify volatile mid-2026 Claude Code claims and CLI flags immediately before publication.
+5. Run a human browser pass at approximately 1440×1000 and 390×844 because the managed browser surface was unavailable during this build.
 
-## Known blockers
+## Blockers
 
-None.
+None for chaptering. Interactive visual QA remains a review follow-up, not a content or path blocker. Git metadata is read-only in this sandbox, so the completed files could not be committed from this session.
